      en: "The Tonkolili Iron Ore Mine, located in central Sierra Leone, stands as one of the largest magnetite deposits in Africa, boasting an estimated resource of approximately 12.8 billion tonnes. Industrial production at the site commenced in 2011 under African Minerals, with the Shandong Iron and Steel Group later assuming full ownership of the operations. The logistics of the mine are supported by a dedicated 200-kilometer railway line that transports processed ore to the Port of Pepel for international distribution. As a cornerstone of Sierra Leone's extractive industry, the mine significantly influences the national GDP and provides critical employment in the Tonkolili District. However, the technical demands of processing magnetite and the maintenance of large-scale infrastructure remain central challenges for the sustainable management of this vast mineral resource.",
